  "_comment_clock_sync": "Measured at LAN setup, one reading per host, folded together by `clocksync --combine`. box-a is the client host and so the reference. NOTE what this does NOT do: offset_ms is subtracted from nothing, because every duration in C-4 and C-5 is single-host and a constant offset cancels in their difference. It is here as evidence that the clocks were disciplined at all. rate_error_ppm is the field that touches a number: box-c's clock ticks 6.5 ppm faster than box-a's, so the pipeline divides n3's worker-local durations by 1.0000065 before taking the residual, which on a two-second service time is 13 microseconds. Absent means NOT MEASURED, never zero.",
